1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,300
I installed Arch to improve my productivity. Obviously.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,933
Then I opened the desktop. Productivity? That can wait.

3
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:17,500
This Omarchy setup brings Arch and Hyprland together in a
Nanally-themed desktop.

4
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:25,700
Wallpaper, windows, terminals. Even the input method
follows the theme. Let's just look for a moment.

5
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:32,800
I thought the makeover ended at the desktop. Then I opened
DSH.

6
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:38,033
Oh, hello. There's a big blue fish living here too.

7
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:45,033
It floats. It glows. And the preview badge now says: Oh,
Whale, Whale...

8
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:51,733
Other AI apps say welcome. My divine whale asks for two
bowls of rice.

9
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:59,900
Pressure me? I'll send a truckload of big fish after you.
No code yet. Plenty of attitude.

10
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:10,000
Now for the best bit. Let's shift the whale into gear.
Reasoning effort becomes a flowing slider.

11
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:17,533
Push it to Max. The skin doesn't add intelligence. But the
ceremony is immaculate.

12
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:26,233
Like the colors? You can switch entire Omarchy palettes.
No need to recolor every little corner.

13
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:32,900
Music, spending reminders, and a file sidebar. The little
touches are all here.

14
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:40,733
Lots of personality. A clear setup: one profile, two local
plugins, and the matching components.

15
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:47,567
Copy the configuration, install the dependencies, and open
DSH. Match the documented versions.

16
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:56,267
The desktop brings the looks. The whale brings the jokes.
Am I more productive? Who knows. I do want to open my
computer more often.
